A||||6||ChadMan||A toast to all of you on St Patrick's Day||||10||
Z||000000||ChadMan||03-17-2000||10:16 AM||||May you be poor in misfortune,<BR>Rich in blessings,<BR>Slow to make enemies,<BR>Quick to make friends.<P>But rich or poor, quick or slow,<BR>May you know nothing but happiness<BR>From this day forward.<P>Like many people of Irish descent, I'm leaving work early for my favorite pub.  Here's to you!  Happy St. Patrick's Day!||||reg||10
Z||000001||loafer87gt||03-17-2000||11:04 AM||||May the luck of the Irish be with you all! If any of you guys happen to be around Birch Hills, Saskatchewan, pop in the ol pub, thats where I'll be. Green beer, MMMMMM...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||03-17-2000||12:02 PM||||Why is it that NYC can make the river(s) green for St. Patricks Day, but can't take the gray out of it the rest of the year?  I have to work, so drink a green beer for me!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spyder||03-17-2000||12:25 PM||||Happy St. Patrick’s Day!!<BR>I spent last St Patrick's day weekend in Savannah , I had so much fun I came home two days late.  <BR>I also had alcohol poisoning.  It usually takes me 3 1/2 hours to drive home, it took me Seven.  I would stop at each exit, vomit, drink a little coke, eat a fourth of a mini powder doughnut and then to the next exit to repeat the process.  <BR>My friends asked me to come back, <BR>I humbly denied. <P>Oh yeah, I used to live in Savannah, they quit dying the river green, environmental issues (LOL)  It Could only help that nasty river.  <BR>They do put green dye in the fountains. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Patrick||03-17-2000||02:22 PM||||<BR>With a name like <I>Patrick</I>, I guess I should be involved with this thread...<P>Yes, my forefathers were Irish. I'm far from the Emerald Isle, but the lush green landscape of British Columbia is a constant reminder to me of my heritage. Of course, there aren't vast cedar rainforests in Ireland, but at least the color is right. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>On St. Patty's Day, everyone is allowed to be Irish. Enjoy!  ||||reg||14
Z||000005||Raydar||03-17-2000||02:38 PM||||I suppose that, since my mother's last name was McGuckin, that I might have a bit of Irish in there, somewhere.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Spyder, Just remember that an Irishman is never drunk so long as he can hang on to a blade of grass, and not fall off the face of the earth. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||03-17-2000||10:13 PM||||I'm more Scottish descent than anything, but I do have a wee bit of Irish in me for sure. I toast everyone a Happy St. Paddy's Day too, regardless if your cup contains green beer or bottled water!||||reg||1
